{"id": "EUVD-2026-55607", "enisaUuid": "59ba4025-c627-33c6-b6af-1fd89206f18c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsched_ext: Don't warn on core-sched forced idle in put_prev_task_scx()\n\nput_prev_task_scx() warns when a runnable task drops to a lower sched_class\nwithout SCX_OPS_ENQ_LAST, on the assumption that balance_one() would have\nkept it running. Core scheduling breaks that: a forced-idle SMT sibling\nreschedules through the core_pick fast path in pick_next_task(), which skips\npick_task_scx() and thus balance_one(), so a runnable task can drop to idle\nwith ENQ_LAST unset.\n\nGate the warning on sched_cpu_cookie_match(): a cookie mismatch means core\nscheduling forced the idle, while a match (or core scheduling off) still\ncatches a genuine missing-ENQ_LAST drop.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:04:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:06", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6267ebee9f2f3e26f4968bf6dc29d350620fa320", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2907e9d0f05b506dfd58aec589a23042a56ef36b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2f188cdbf8312289532c36eb4e9eb1c9544d43a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b7d9c359e5cf867f7eb23df3bb1c6b9e58af24da"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wg3q-w98j-244c", "CVE-2026-68421"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "029e720d-2145-3673-9e70-7daa587f9f06", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "0302cfcb-bb73-39ae-83a4-0dcd23544c5d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "18c0e966-3648-35e6-b4fb-2d11fb32d3d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7c65ae81ea86a6ed8086e1a5651acd766187f19b <6267ebee9f2f3e26f4968bf6dc29d350620fa320"}, {"id": "1fd2a437-544c-34b2-8333-e2dd0cf14be1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "22a39d8a-c32a-3341-a581-1cfcaffb736e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7c65ae81ea86a6ed8086e1a5651acd766187f19b <e2f188cdbf8312289532c36eb4e9eb1c9544d43a"}, {"id": "271f2bca-609e-3813-bd5e-bc0293747364", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.6"}, {"id": "53549521-2012-3c07-9302-f65e9c307d8f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "591f6a45-6f74-39de-bc83-a9a37bf551f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "64514679-4bc9-3ced-9295-443f9e603daa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7c65ae81ea86a6ed8086e1a5651acd766187f19b <b7d9c359e5cf867f7eb23df3bb1c6b9e58af24da"}, {"id": "b089b055-197c-3276-9191-79c35904fa32", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7c65ae81ea86a6ed8086e1a5651acd766187f19b <2907e9d0f05b506dfd58aec589a23042a56ef36b"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "522930cd-cce6-3635-819d-f54ed08afdde", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}